ments: Recruitment -> \\\"Recruitment Simulation\\\" / \\\"Simulate candidate profiles and hiring decisions\\\" / technical -1, behavioral +10%, domain -1; Training -> \\\"Training Simulation\\\" / \\\"Model the impact of training programs\\\" / technical +1, domain +1; Promotion -> \\\"Promotion Simulation\\\" / technical -5%, behavioral +10%. Tab data-state switches active/inactive correctly.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Category adjustment sliders are usable and display their value correctly (Technical Level Change driven -1 -> 0 -> +2 -> -2, Weight Change -> -30%). Run Simulation with technical +2 / behavioral +10% weight / domain -1 updated all outputs: Coverage 68%->82%, Avg Level 3.3->4.0 (Advanced), Critical Path list re-ordered, Risk Gaps 0 with \\\"Model Healthy\\\" summary. A further run with technical -2/-30% gave Coverage 60%, Avg 2.8, Critical Path 4. Reset restored the original model exactly: Coverage 68%, Avg 3.3, Critical Path 3, Risk Gaps 0 and all six competencies back to Advanced/90%, Intermediate/80%, Intermediate/60%, Advanced/90%, Intermediate/70%, Intermediate/50%.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Saved model edits are not persisted; state reverts to defaults on leaving/reopening or reloading\", \"actual\": \"Edited Software Engineer (Agile Methodology -> level 5), which moved Coverage 68%->73% and Avg Level 3.3->3.7. Clicking Save showed a \\\"Model Saved - Your changes have been saved successfully.\\\" toast, but localStorage and sessionStorage both stayed completely empty (0 keys). Navigating back to the model list and reopening Software Engineer restored the defaults: Coverage 68%, Avg Level 3.3, Agile Methodology back to \\\"Intermediate\\\". Reloading the app and reopening the model gave the same default state, so no levels, weights or enabled states are restored.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Direct edits are bounded by construction: each node exposes exactly 5 level buttons (set-level-1..5) and the weight slider reports aria-valuemin=10 / aria-valuemax=100. Simulation clamps at both ends, verified numerically: technical +2 on a level-4 competency gave Avg 4.0 (requires cap at 5, not 6); behavioral +10% on a 100% weight kept Coverage 60% (cap at 100, not 110); a further compounding run produced Coverage 52% / Avg 1.8, which matches the clamped model (agile level 0->1, code-review weight 0->10) exactly, versus 50% / 1.7 if unclamped.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"No reload needed in any case. Level: Collaboration -> level 5 moved Coverage 65%->75% and progress bar translateX -34.86%->-25.45%. Enabled: disabling Programming Languages moved Coverage 68%->65% and bar to -34.86%. Weight: Code Review weight edits moved bar -31.72%->-31.32% and Coverage 68%->69%. Coverage text and the role=progressbar indicator stayed mutually consistent throughout.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Initially selected Recruitment scenario loads with uninitialized (all-zero) adjustments, so running it does nothing\", \"actual\": \"On first load the Recruitment tab is active but all four category adjustments display Level Change 0 / Weight Change 0% (sliders centred at aria-valuenow 2 of 0-4 and 30 of 0-60, i.e. zero deltas). Clicking Run Simulation without switching tabs left every output unchanged: Coverage 68%, Avg Level 3.3, Critical Path 3, Risk Gaps 0 - identical to before. Only after switching to another tab and back does Recruitment show its actual defaults (technical -1/0%, behavioral 0/+10%, leadership 0/0%, domain -1/0%), proving the initial scenario state was never initialized.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Graph controls never show the post-edit state; node 